    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d711-a1">

                <pb facs="0872" n="784" xml:id="pg784"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Translation]<anchor n="92" xml:id="d711-f1"
                        /></seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Haitian Secretary of State for Foreign
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laleau</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the American Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-31">31 October, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: In reply to your note of 31
                    October, 1933, I have the honor to inform you that I am authorized to state that
                    the Haitian Government will not interpret the provisions of paragraph 1, article
                    17, of the law of 4 July, 1933, for budget and public accounting, in such a way
                    as to alter the present practice and procedure regarding the methods effecting
                    restitutions which is the subject of this article. Also it is the understanding
                    of my Government that no omission in the aforesaid law will be considered as
                    affecting the functions and attributions of the Financial Adviser-General
                    Receiver, as defined by the treaty of 16 September, 1915, and the accords
                    relative thereto.</p>
                <p>I take [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">León Laleau</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
